    :hasColorIdentity :White ;
    :hasColorIdentity :Blue ;
    :hasColorIdentity :Red ;
    :isInSet :ModernHorizons3Commander ;
    :cardNumber "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    :artist "Aaron Miller" ;
    :hasLanguage :English ;
    :power "3" ;
    :powerValue "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    :toughness "5" ;
    :toughnessValue "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Haste ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Menace ;
    :printedText """Menace, haste
Whenever Satya attacks, create a tapped and attacking token that's a copy of up to one other target nontoken creature you control. You get {E}{E} (two energy counters). At the beginning of the next end step, sacrifice that token unless you pay an amount of {E} equal to its mana value."""@en ;
    :oracleText """Menace, haste
Whenever Satya attacks, create a tapped and attacking token that's a copy of up to one other target nontoken creature you control. You get {E}{E} (two energy counters). At the beginning of the next end step, sacrifice that token unless you pay an amount of {E} equal to its mana value."""@en ;
    :gathererUrl "https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=665304"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :scryfallUrl "https://scryfall.com/card/m3c/3/satya-aetherflux-genius"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :hasLegality
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Commander ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Standard ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Modern ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Legacy ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Vintage ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pioneer ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pauper ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ;
    :hasRuling
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Energy counters aren't mana. They don't go away as steps, phases, and turns end, and effects that add mana "of any type" can't give you energy counters."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Some triggered abilities that state that you "may pay" a certain amount of {E} describe an effect that happens "If you do." In that case, no player may take actions to try to stop the ability's effect after you make your choice. If the payment is followed by the phrase "When you do," then you'll choose any targets for that reflexive triggered ability and put it on the stack before players can take actions."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Energy counters are a kind of counter that a player may have. They're not associated with any specific permanents."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Any enters-the-battlefield abilities of the copied creature will trigger when the token enters the battlefield. Any "as [this creature] enters the battlefield" or "[this creature] enters the battlefield with" abilities of the creature will also work."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You choose which player, planeswalker, or battle the token is attacking as you create the token. It doesn't need to be attacking the same player, planeswalker, or battle that Satya is attacking."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """{E} is the energy symbol. It represents one energy counter."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If the copied creature is copying something else, then the token enters the battlefield as whatever that creature copied."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Keep track of how many energy counters each player has. Potential ways to track this include writing theme down on paper or using dice, but any method that is clear and mutually agreeable is fine. (At higher levels of tournament play, dice may not be allowed for tracking counters that players have.)"""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If an effect says you get one or more {E}, you get that many energy counters. To pay one or more {E}, you lose that many energy counters. You can't pay more energy counters than you have. Any effects that interact with counters a player gets, has, or loses can interact with energy counters."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If a spell or ability with one or more targets states that you "may pay" some amount of {E}, and each permanent that it targets has become an illegal target, the spell or ability won't resolve. You can't pay any {E} even if you want to."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If the copied creature has {X} in its mana cost, X is 0."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Some triggered abilities state that you "may pay" a certain amount of {E}. You can't pay that amount multiple times to multiply the effect. You simply choose whether or not to pay that amount of {E} as the ability resolves."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Some spells and abilities that give you {E} may require targets. If each target chosen is an illegal target as that spell or ability tries to resolve, it won't resolve. You won't get any {E}."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The token copies exactly what was printed on the original card and nothing else (unless that creature is itself copying something else; see below). It doesn't copy whether that creature is tapped or untapped, whether it has any counters on it or Auras attached to it, or any non-copy effects that have changed its power, toughness, types, color, and so on."""@en ] .

:CaythFamedMechanist rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  :Card ;
    :cardName "Cayth, Famed Mechanist" ;
    :manaCost "{1}{U}{R}{W}" ;
    :manaValue "4"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    :hasSuperType :Legendary ;
    :hasCardType :Creature ;
    :hasSubType :Dwarf ;
    :hasSubType :Artificer ;
    :hasRarity :MythicRare ;
    :hasColor :White ;
    :hasColor :Blue ;
    :hasColor :Red ;
    :hasColorIdentity :White ;
    :hasColorIdentity :Blue ;
    :hasColorIdentity :Red ;
    :isInSet :ModernHorizons3Commander ;
    :cardNumber "6"^^xsd:integer ;
    :artist "Eric Wilkerson" ;
    :hasLanguage :English ;
    :power "3" ;
    :powerValue "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    :toughness "3" ;
    :toughnessValue "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    :hasKeywordAction :Proliferate ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Fabricate ;
    :hasKeywordAction :Populate ;
    :printedText """Fabricate 1 (When this creature enters, put a +1/+1 counter on it or create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token.)
Other nontoken creatures you control have fabricate 1.
{2}, {T}: Choose one —
• Populate.
• Proliferate."""@en ;
    :oracleText """Fabricate 1 (When this creature enters, put a +1/+1 counter on it or create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token.)
Other nontoken creatures you control have fabricate 1.
{2}, {T}: Choose one —
• Populate.
• Proliferate."""@en ;
    :gathererUrl "https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=665327"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :scryfallUrl "https://scryfall.com/card/m3c/6/cayth-famed-mechanist"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :hasLegality
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Commander ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Standard ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Modern ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Legacy ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Vintage ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pioneer ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pauper ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ;
    :hasRuling
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If a player or permanent has more than one kind of counter on it, and you choose for it to get additional counters, it must get one of each kind of counter it already has. You can't have it get just one kind of counter it already has and not the others."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Fabricate doesn't cause the creature with the ability to enter the battlefield with +1/+1 counters already on it. For example, Cayth, Famed Machinist will enter the battlefield as a 3/3 creature, then its fabricate ability goes on the stack. Players may take actions (such as casting instants) while the ability is waiting to resolve."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You choose whether to put a +1/+1 counter on the creature or create a Servo token as the fabricate ability is resolving. No player may take actions between the time you choose and the time that the counter is added or the token is created."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Any "as [this creature] enters the battlefield" or "[this creature] enters the battlefield with" abilities of the new token will work."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If you control no creature tokens when you populate, nothing will happen."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The new creature token copies the characteristics of the original token as stated by the effect that created the original token."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The new token doesn't copy whether the original token is tapped or untapped, whether it has any counters on it or Auras and Equipment attached to it, or any non-copy effects that have changed its power, toughness, color, and so on."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You don't have to choose every permanent or player that has a counter—only the ones you want to add counters to. Since "any number" includes zero, you don't have to choose any permanents at all, and you don't have to choose any players at all."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If you can't put a +1/+1 counter on the creature for any reason as fabricate resolves (for instance, if it's no longer on the battlefield), you just create a Servo token."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Players can respond to a spell or ability whose effect includes proliferating. Once that spell or ability starts to resolve, however, and its controller chooses which permanents and players will get new counters, it's too late for anyone to respond."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """When you proliferate, you can choose any permanent that has a counter, including ones controlled by opponents. You can choose any player who has a counter, including opponents. You can't choose cards in any zone other than the battlefield, even if they have counters on them."""@en ] .

:AuroraShifter rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
