    :isInSet :ModernHorizons3Commander ;
    :cardNumber "95"^^xsd:integer ;
    :artist "José Parodi" ;
    :hasLanguage :English ;
    :power "9" ;
    :powerValue "9"^^xsd:integer ;
    :toughness "9" ;
    :toughnessValue "9"^^xsd:integer ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Flying ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Vigilance ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Unearth ;
    :hasKeywordAbility :Trample ;
    :printedText """Flying, vigilance, trample
Whenever you attack, other creatures you control get +2/+2 and gain indestructible until end of turn.
Unearth—Pay eight {E}. (Pay eight energy counters: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)"""@en ;
    :oracleText """Flying, vigilance, trample
Whenever you attack, other creatures you control get +2/+2 and gain indestructible until end of turn.
Unearth—Pay eight {E}. (Pay eight energy counters: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)"""@en ;
    :gathererUrl "https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=665369"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :scryfallUrl "https://scryfall.com/card/m3c/95/salvation-colossus"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :hasLegality
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Commander ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Standard ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Modern ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Legacy ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Vintage ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pioneer ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pauper ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ;
    :hasRuling
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If you activate a card's unearth ability but that card is removed from your graveyard before the ability resolves, that unearth ability will do nothing as it resolves."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Some triggered abilities that state that you "may pay" a certain amount of {E} describe an effect that happens "If you do." In that case, no player may take actions to try to stop the ability's effect after you make your choice. If the payment is followed by the phrase "When you do," then you'll choose any targets for that reflexive triggered ability and put it on the stack before players can take actions."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Energy counters are a kind of counter that a player may have. They're not associated with any specific permanents."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If an effect says you get one or more {E}, you get that many energy counters. To pay one or more {E}, you lose that many energy counters. You can't pay more energy counters than you have. Any effects that interact with counters a player gets, has, or loses can interact with energy counters."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If a permanent returned to the battlefield with unearth would leave the battlefield for any reason, it's exiled instead—unless the spell or ability that's causing the permanent to leave the battlefield is actually trying to exile it! In that case, it succeeds at exiling it. If that spell or ability later returns the card to the battlefield (as Static Prison might, for example), the permanent card will return to the battlefield as a new object with no relation to its previous existence. The unearth effects will no longer apply to it."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Unearth grants haste to the permanent that's returned to the battlefield (even if it's not a creature card). However, neither of the "exile" abilities is granted to that permanent. If that permanent loses all its abilities, it will still be exiled at the beginning of the next end step, and if it would leave the battlefield, it is still exiled instead."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If a spell or ability with one or more targets states that you "may pay" some amount of {E}, and each permanent that it targets has become an illegal target, the spell or ability won't resolve. You can't pay any {E} even if you want to."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """{E} is the energy symbol. It represents one energy counter."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """At the beginning of the next end step, a permanent returned to the battlefield with unearth is exiled. This is a delayed triggered ability, and it can be countered by effects that counter triggered abilities. If the ability is countered, the permanent will stay on the battlefield and the delayed triggered ability won't trigger again. However, the replacement effect will still exile the permanent if it eventually leaves the battlefield."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Some spells and abilities that give you {E} may require targets. If each target chosen is an illegal target as that spell or ability tries to resolve, it won't resolve. You won't get any {E}."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Energy counters aren't mana. They don't go away as steps, phases, and turns end, and effects that add mana "of any type" can't give you energy counters."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Some triggered abilities state that you "may pay" a certain amount of {E}. You can't pay that amount multiple times to multiply the effect. You simply choose whether or not to pay that amount of {E} as the ability resolves."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Keep track of how many energy counters each player has. Potential ways to track this include writing theme down on paper or using dice, but any method that is clear and mutually agreeable is fine. (At higher levels of tournament play, dice may not be allowed for tracking counters that players have.)"""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Activating a card's unearth ability isn't the same as casting that card. The unearth ability is put on the stack, but the card is not. Spells and abilities that interact with activated abilities will interact with unearth, but spells and abilities that interact with spells (such as Flare of Denial) will not."""@en ] .

:SilverquillLecturer rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  :Card ;
    :cardName "Silverquill Lecturer" ;
    :manaCost "{4}{W}" ;
    :manaValue "5"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    :hasCardType :Creature ;
    :hasSubType :Kor ;
    :hasSubType :Wizard ;
    :hasRarity :Rare ;
    :hasColor :White ;
    :hasColorIdentity :White ;
    :isInSet :ModernHorizons3Commander ;
    :cardNumber "96"^^xsd:integer ;
    :artist "Ryan Pancoast" ;
    :hasLanguage :English ;
    :power "3" ;
    :powerValue "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    :toughness "3" ;
    :toughnessValue "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    :printedText """Creature spells you cast have demonstrate. (Whenever you cast a creature spell, you may copy it. If you do, choose an opponent to also copy it. Each copy becomes a token.)"""@en ;
    :oracleText """Creature spells you cast have demonstrate. (Whenever you cast a creature spell, you may copy it. If you do, choose an opponent to also copy it. Each copy becomes a token.)"""@en ;
    :flavorText """"Did you bring enough to share with the rest of the class?\""""@en ;
    :gathererUrl "https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=665370"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :scryfallUrl "https://scryfall.com/card/m3c/96/silverquill-lecturer"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :hasLegality
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Commander ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Standard ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Modern ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Legacy ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Vintage ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pioneer ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pauper ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ;
    :hasRuling
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Resolving copies of permanent spells become tokens as they enter the battlefield. These tokens are not considered "created" when this happens."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If you cast a spell with demonstrate and both you and an opponent copy it, the opponent's copy will resolve first, then your copy will resolve, and finally the original spell will resolve."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You choose whether to make a copy as the demonstrate ability resolves. This happens before the original spell resolves. Your copy goes on the stack above the original spell."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If you cast the spell and choose not to copy it, no opponent will get to copy it either."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If you copy a spell with demonstrate, you then immediately choose an opponent. If they copy the spell, it goes on top of the stack."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If any additional or alternative costs were paid to cast the spell with demonstrate, the copies will see those choices as well. For example, if the spell has a kicker ability and was kicked, the copies will also be kicked"""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If the spell had an X value chosen for it as it was cast, the copies will have the same value of X."""@en ] .

:AuroraShifterModernHorizons3Commander97 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  :Card ;
    :cardName "Aurora Shifter" ;
    :manaCost "{1}{U}" ;
    :manaValue "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    :hasCardType :Creature ;
    :hasSubType :Shapeshifter ;
    :hasRarity :Rare ;
    :hasColor :Blue ;
    :hasColorIdentity :Blue ;
    :isInSet :ModernHorizons3Commander ;
    :cardNumber "97"^^xsd:integer ;
    :artist "Justyna Dura" ;
    :hasLanguage :English ;
    :power "1" ;
    :powerValue "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    :toughness "3" ;
    :toughnessValue "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    :printedText """Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, you get that many {E}.
At the beginning of combat on your turn, you may pay {E}{E}. When you do, this creature becomes a copy of another target creature you control, except it has this ability and "Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, you get that many {E}.\""""@en ;
    :oracleText """Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, you get that many {E}.
At the beginning of combat on your turn, you may pay {E}{E}. When you do, this creature becomes a copy of another target creature you control, except it has this ability and "Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, you get that many {E}.\""""@en ;
    :gathererUrl "https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=665371"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :scryfallUrl "https://scryfall.com/card/m3c/97/aurora-shifter"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :hasLegality
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Commander ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Standard ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Modern ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Legacy ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Vintage ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pioneer ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pauper ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ;
    :hasRuling
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If a spell or ability with one or more targets states that you "may pay" some amount of {E}, and each permanent that it targets has become an illegal target, the spell or ability won't resolve. You can't pay any {E} even if you want to."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Some spells and abilities that give you {E} may require targets. If each target chosen is an illegal target as that spell or ability tries to resolve, it won't resolve. You won't get any {E}."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If the copied creature is copying something else, then Aurora Shifter becomes a copy of whatever that creature copied (with the listed exception)."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Energy counters are a kind of counter that a player may have. They're not associated with any specific permanents."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If the copied creature has {X} in its mana cost, X is 0."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Keep track of how many energy counters each player has. Potential ways to track this include writing theme down on paper or using dice, but any method that is clear and mutually agreeable is fine. (At higher levels of tournament play, dice may not be allowed for tracking counters that players have.)"""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Some triggered abilities that state that you "may pay" a certain amount of {E} describe an effect that happens "If you do." In that case, no player may take actions to try to stop the ability's effect after you make your choice. If the payment is followed by the phrase "When you do," then you'll choose any targets for that reflexive triggered ability and put it on the stack before players can take actions."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Energy counters aren't mana. They don't go away as steps, phases, and turns end, and effects that add mana "of any type" can't give you energy counters."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Because Aurora Shifter isn't entering the battlefield when it becomes a copy of another creature, any "When [this creature] enters the battlefield" or "[This creature] enters the battlefield with" abilities of the copied creature won't apply."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """{E} is the energy symbol. It represents one energy counter."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """You don't choose a target for Aurora Shifter's last ability at the time it triggers. Rather, a second "reflexive" ability triggers when you pay {E}{E} this way. You choose a target for that ability as it goes on the stack. Each player may respond to this triggered ability as normal."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Aurora Shifter copies exactly what was printed on the original creature and nothing else, with the listed exception (unless that permanent is copying something else; see below). It doesn't copy whether that creature is tapped or untapped, whether it has any counters on it or Auras and Equipment attached to it, and so on."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If an effect says you get one or more {E}, you get that many energy counters. To pay one or more {E}, you lose that many energy counters. You can't pay more energy counters than you have. Any effects that interact with counters a player gets, has, or loses can interact with energy counters."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2024-06-07"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Some triggered abilities state that you "may pay" a certain amount of {E}. You can't pay that amount multiple times to multiply the effect. You simply choose whether or not to pay that amount of {E} as the ability resolves."""@en ] .

